      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed toward the dark door, his face as craggy as tree bark. Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the very last apple of the season, polished and red. She set it on the step between them as a thank you for his guidance. Mosk stared at the fruit for a long time before he stood up, tied his vest tight, and began to lead her down the first stair."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
