{
  "bridge_text": "Since Lina could not turn away from a mystery she had only just begun to uncover, she stood her ground before the old fox.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed sternly at the door, but Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season. She set it on the step between them and said it was for the trouble of walking her down. Mosk stared at the fruit for a long time before he finally stood up, tied his vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming became a quiet song, and a firefly the size of a robin lay on a bed of moss. Her glow was almost out. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he whispered that she had been his friend once, but he had failed to bring her medicine long ago. He had been guarding this tree ever since, too ashamed to face her."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The secret of Mosk's heart remains tucked away for now, just as he stood there in silence, considering that bright red apple on the step.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk looked at the gift for a long time before he finally stood up. He tied his vest tight and stepped onto the first stair without a word, beckoning Lina to follow him down into the shadows of the hollow tree."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The weight of a long-held regret is a heavy burden to carry through the dark. Yet, even in the quietest, saddest corners of the Hollow Tree, hope has a way of finding its footing.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt by the mossy bed and softly asked the firefly queen what might help her light return. A drop of warm milk and a kind word, the queen replied, for that was the truest medicine of all. Mosk hurried to fetch a thimble of milk and gently laid his paw beside hers, his long-held shame finally beginning to lift. As the queen's glow steadied and grew bright, the humming in the tree became a beautiful new tune, and Mosk found himself humming along."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s5"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The wind outside the hollow tree may whisper of many things, but here in the shadows, only the fox and the girl remain. Let us return to that spiral of stairs where Mosk waits.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree, Lina discovered a winding staircase of wood and stone, and there sat an old grey fox named Mosk. He wore a patched green vest and spoke with a voice like dry leaves, warning her to turn back and forget the humming. But Lina stood her ground, telling the old fox that she could never forget a secret she had only just begun to uncover."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Even with a shiver of caution in her heart, Lina stood her ground before the fox in the green vest. She knew that sometimes, facing a stranger requires a steady spirit and a very kind gesture.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Mosk told her, in a voice like dry leaves, that the tree was not for visiting and that she should go home and forget the humming. Lina looked at the old fox and said she could not forget what she had not yet heard."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed at the door, but Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season. She set it on the step between them and said this was for the trouble of walking her down. Mosk stared at the apple for a long time before he stood up, tied his vest, and stepped onto the first stair."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The secrets of the hollow tree are many, but even a silent guardian like Mosk cannot ignore the sweetness of a gift.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk stared at that bright red apple for a long time, his eyes reflecting its polished skin. Then he stood up, tied his vest tight, and stepped onto the first stair without a word, beckoning Lina to follow him down into the cool shadows."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
